# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Aeris — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env.local. The UI starts without secrets, but live
# aircraft data stays disabled until an operator configures an authorized source.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Authorized ADS-B relay -------------------------------------------------
# Server-only HTTP origin and bearer token. Do not expose either to the browser.
# FLIGHT_DATA_ORIGIN=
# FLIGHT_RELAY_HTTP_TOKEN=

# Base64url Ed25519 seed (32 bytes) or PKCS#8 private key used only by the
# same-origin stream-ticket route. Configure the matching public key on relay.
# FLIGHT_STREAM_PRIVATE_KEY=

# Browser-visible direct WebSocket endpoint. Use wss outside local development.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FLIGHT_STREAM_URL=

# Exact public application origin checked by the ticket issuer.
# FLIGHT_APP_ORIGIN=

# Provider attribution displayed in the application.
# FLIGHT_DATA_ATTRIBUTION_PROVIDER=
# FLIGHT_DATA_ATTRIBUTION_LABEL=
# FLIGHT_DATA_ATTRIBUTION_URL=

# Optional ticket issuance limit. Keep operational values in private config.
# FLIGHT_TICKET_ISSUE_LIMIT=

# --- Separately authorized direct providers (legacy development mode) -------
# Leave these blank unless written terms authorize every enabled provider for
# access, processing, retention, display, and downstream use. The server value
# must be set to "authorized" and the browser value to "true" to opt in.
# FLIGHT_DIRECT_PROVIDER_ACCESS=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTHORIZED_DIRECT_FLIGHT_DATA=

# --- Analytics (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# Google Analytics 4 measurement ID. Leave blank to disable analytics.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# --- OpenSky Network (separate authorization required) ----------------------
# OAuth2 client credentials for the server-side trace fallback
# (src/lib/trails/source/server-trace-service.ts). Without these, Aeris
# is available only when the direct-provider authorization gates above are
# enabled. Provide both credential values or neither.
#
# Create a client at https://opensky-network.org/my-opensky (Account → API).
# OPENSKY_CLIENT_ID=
# OPENSKY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- OpenAIP (optional) -----------------------------------------------------
# API key for the airspace vector-tile proxy
# (src/app/api/airspace-tiles/route.ts). Without this, the airspace
# overlay toggle will produce empty responses; flight rendering is
# unaffected. Get a key from https://www.openaip.net (Account → API keys).
#
# Remember: OpenAIP data is CC BY-NC 4.0 — attribution is already rendered
# in-app but non-commercial use is on you.
# OPENAIP_API_KEY=

# --- Data-rights notice ------------------------------------------------------
# This configuration grants no rights to third-party aircraft data. Obtain
# authorization before enabling any provider or relay.
